nd the `1.0 + depth*0.1` factor are all preserved verbatim, using `f64::sqrt`.\n\n8. **Wrapping arithmetic**: integer ops that could overflow in C's signed-int domain use `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add` to avoid Rust panics in debug mode while still matching the C two's-complement result in release mode.\n\n9. **Error-check ordering**: each `case` branch validates `find_node_by_id` first and returns the corresponding `STATUS_ERROR | 0o0XX` constant before doing any other work, matching the C exactly.\n\n10. **Unused statics/helpers**: `add_node`, `initialize_test_data`, and `STATUS_WARNING`/`STATUS_CRITICAL` are kept (marked `#[allow(dead_code)]`) so the translation remains structurally faithful, even though only `jumpnode` is exported."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":22724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18f33547-76a5-4f69-97a3-c8bd279b3bb4","uuid":"146883e0-47bd-423c-ae82-df582239c9f6"}
